.TH ITCMDR\-CLI 1 "" "itcmdr" "itcmdr manual"
.SH NAME
itcmdr\-cli \- site server administration on the server itself
.SH ITCMDR\-CLI
.nf
itcmdr server administration
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-cli [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
\&
Commands:
  help            The guides (docs/) in the terminal: `help` lists topics, `help <topic>` prints one
  init            First\-run setup: prints the 24 recovery words ONCE. Do this in person at the server
  recover\-db\-key  Restore keys/db.key from the escrow with the words (replacement machine)
  keys            Key management
  service         Register a service plugin client key (certified with the words)
  plugins         Service plugin packages (also available as `service plugins ...`)
  user            Users (people with app access)
  backup          Backups (decision 13)
  config          Runtime settings stored in the DB (override server.json): backup.dir, backup.hour, ...
  schedule        Scheduled runs (decision 14)
  cutover         Nightly task \-> default schedule cutover (v0.11.0): status, switch (gated), rollback
  upgrade         Agent self\-upgrade through the rings (v0.21.0): status, start, pause, resume, abort
  auth            Auth mode (v0.12.0 migration from the shared token to signed requests)
  setup           Install and first\-run setup (v0.14.0): checks, site values, master key + first admin key
  restore         Restore an archive into the data dir. Stop the server first
  restore\-stage   Restore through the running server (the app's StageRestore path): the server verifies the archive, then itcmdr\-restore stops the service, restores, restarts and health\-checks, and rolls back on failure. Words on stdin. Signed with this server's root key (owner)
  restore\-status  State of the last app/StageRestore restore
  calls           Call log (v0.15.0): one row per RPC, newest first. Same data as the app's Calls view
  alerts          Site alerts (v0.16.0): list, ack, resolve, silence. Same data as the app's Alerts screen
  agent           Rust agents (v0.17.0): enrollment tokens, list, revoke, maintenance
  adminsvr        Offsite adminsvr link (v0.19.0): enroll, status, unlink, share\-names, allow. In person on the site server
\&
Options:
      \-\-data\-dir <DATA_DIR>  Data dir override (beats ITCMDR_DATA_DIR and server.json)
      \-\-json                 Print JSON instead of text
      \-\-plain\-http           v1.1.0: talk to the local server over plain HTTP instead of HTTPS (not encrypted; explicit opt\-in)
  \-h, \-\-help                 Print help
  \-V, \-\-version              Print version
.fi
