.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-cli keys
.nf
Key management
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-cli keys [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
\&
Commands:
  certify   OFFLINE: certify an existing public key (hex) with the words. Prints a key bundle (JSON)
  new       OFFLINE: generate a keypair and certify it. Private key \-> FILE, bundle \-> FILE.pub.json
  register  Register a certified key bundle on this server
  list      List registered keys
  revoke    Revoke a key by fingerprint (takes effect immediately)
  rotate    Replace a key: new keypair, same kind/name/role, certified with the words; old one revoked
\&
Options:
      \-\-data\-dir <DATA_DIR>  Data dir override (beats ITCMDR_DATA_DIR and server.json)
      \-\-json                 Print JSON instead of text
      \-\-plain\-http           v1.1.0: talk to the local server over plain HTTP instead of HTTPS (not encrypted; explicit opt\-in)
  \-h, \-\-help                 Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-cli keys certify
.nf
OFFLINE: certify an existing public key (hex) with the words. Prints a key bundle (JSON)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-cli keys certify [OPTIONS] \-\-kind <KIND> \-\-name <NAME> \-\-role <ROLE> \-\-public\-key <PUBLIC_KEY>
\&
Options:
      \-\-data\-dir <DATA_DIR>      Data dir override (beats ITCMDR_DATA_DIR and server.json)
      \-\-kind <KIND>              [possible values: client, user]
      \-\-json                     Print JSON instead of text
      \-\-name <NAME>              
      \-\-plain\-http               v1.1.0: talk to the local server over plain HTTP instead of HTTPS (not encrypted; explicit opt\-in)
      \-\-role <ROLE>              [possible values: owner, admin, user, client]
      \-\-public\-key <PUBLIC_KEY>  
      \-\-out <OUT>                Write the bundle here instead of stdout
  \-h, \-\-help                     Print help
.fi
