.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-cli backup
.nf
Backups (decision 13)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-cli backup [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
\&
Commands:
  create  Take a backup now
  list    List archives, newest first
  verify  Check an archive's signature and hash; \-\-deep also decrypts it with the words and checks every file against the manifest
  drill   Restore drill (v0.22.0): copy the newest archive to a temp folder, check it against this server's master key, delete the copy and report. \-\-deep also decrypts it with the words (the monthly drill). Everything stays on this machine
  prune   Apply nightly retention now
\&
Options:
      \-\-data\-dir <DATA_DIR>  Data dir override (beats ITCMDR_DATA_DIR and server.json)
      \-\-json                 Print JSON instead of text
      \-\-plain\-http           v1.1.0: talk to the local server over plain HTTP instead of HTTPS (not encrypted; explicit opt\-in)
  \-h, \-\-help                 Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-cli backup create
.nf
