.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-cli upgrade
.nf
Agent self\-upgrade through the rings (v0.21.0): status, start, pause, resume, abort
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-cli upgrade [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
\&
Commands:
  status        The current rollout (version, ring, state, what holds the ring) and the last few
  start         Roll an installed, owner\-signed itcmdr\-agent\-release out, starting at ring 0
  pause         Pause the rollout (no new offers)
  resume        Resume a paused rollout (the ring soaks again; failed machines are offered it again)
  abort         Abort the rollout (machines already upgraded stay upgraded)
  server\-start  Upgrade this server to an installed, owner\-signed itcmdr\-server\-release (in the update window unless \-\-now; the server watchdog swaps it in and rolls back when unhealthy)
  server\-abort  Cancel a server upgrade that is still waiting for the window
  restore\-db    Watchdog rollback step: put the pre\-upgrade database safety copy back (server stopped)
\&
Options:
      \-\-data\-dir <DATA_DIR>  Data dir override (beats ITCMDR_DATA_DIR and server.json)
      \-\-json                 Print JSON instead of text
      \-\-plain\-http           v1.1.0: talk to the local server over plain HTTP instead of HTTPS (not encrypted; explicit opt\-in)
  \-h, \-\-help                 Print help
.fi
