.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-cli setup apply
.nf
Write site values into server.json (created when missing). Upgrades pass \-\-keep\-existing, which only fills values that are missing or empty
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-cli setup apply [OPTIONS]
\&
Options:
      \-\-logs\-dir <LOGS_DIR>
          The maintenanceRuns share/folder the agents write to
      \-\-data\-dir <DATA_DIR>
          
      \-\-json
          Print JSON instead of text
      \-\-backup\-dir <BACKUP_DIR>
          Backup folder (a share or second disk)
      \-\-plain\-http
          v1.1.0: talk to the local server over plain HTTP instead of HTTPS (not encrypted; explicit opt\-in)
      \-\-bind\-addr <BIND_ADDR>
          
      \-\-api\-plain\-http <API_PLAIN_HTTP>
          Also accept plain HTTP (unencrypted) from other machines: `true` or `false`. HTTPS is always on; plain HTTP from this machine always works. For v1.0 apps until they update [possible values: true, false]
      \-\-keep\-existing
          
      \-\-config <CONFIG>
          server.json to write (default: the one in use, else %ProgramData%\\itcmdr\\server.json)
  \-h, \-\-help
          Print help
.fi
